  "final_text": "I built the dashboard and created the alert rule, and both now exist in Kibana. The rule has not fired or been tested yet. I tried to check that its search actually matches the sample data's 5xx requests, but Kibana's console proxy is turned off on this instance.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` data view (time field `timestamp`) covers web access logs:\n- **Who made the request:** `clientip`, `agent`, `machine.os`.\n- **What was requested:** `url`, `request`, `extension`, `referer`.\n- **The result:** `response`, which is the HTTP status code stored as text with a keyword copy, and `bytes`.\n- **Where from and to:** `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`.\n- **Other:** `tags`, `memory` and `hour_of_day`.\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-62fc3433 Web logs overview\"** has 7 panels:\n- Total requests\n- Unique visitors (distinct client IPs)\n- Total bytes served\n- Requests over time, split by response code\n- Share of each response code (pie chart)\n- Top 10 URLs, with request count and bytes\n- Top 10 source countries\n\nLink: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-62fc3433-web-logs-overview-1c7030342ad6\n\n**3. Alert rule \"EFF-62fc3433 5xx spike\"** (id `43c0fa86-4fa2-463c-bd9c-6ac7659ced85`):\n- It runs every minute against `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- It counts requests whose `response.keyword` is between \"500\" and \"599\" over the last 5 minutes, and fires when that count is above 10.\n- Kibana confirms it is saved and enabled. Its first run was still pending when I checked.\n- It has no notification actions, so it will create alerts but not send anything. You'd need to add a connector, such as Slack or email, for that.\n\nThe 500\u2013599 range is a text comparison, not a numeric one. It works because status codes are always three digits.",
